#>wonder_syntax_profile_stack_1
?["After the Spw.l newline preprocess, do parse spans still point at the raw source, or at the collapsed text?"]{
  #:depth #!computational
  ~#hypothesis: "offsets can coincide for a single newline but line and column describe the collapsed text, so editors would mis-place diagnostics"
  !probe{ "parse '@dialect:Spw.l\\nfoo bar\\nbaz {\\n  x\\n}\\n' and read the span of the baz node against src.indexOf('baz'); on 2026-10-12 the offset matched (23) but the span said line 1 column 24 where the raw source has line 3 column 1, and the preprocessed text was 33 characters against 35 raw" }
  $%[span.offset_delta, span.line_delta, product.dialectPreprocessed]
}
